2026-08-30T11:42Z claude note filed on 0481's verdict: every fidelity/recall cell of the 0264 campaign ran on CPU because the harness dropped --device. The fix is merged (PR #102); this ticket spends it. 0267 must not quote any bench/results/0264-gpu-arm/ fidelity figure as a GPU number until this lands.

--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0481 isolated the 0264 anomaly: `bench/sweep.py` never forwarded
`--device` to the fidelity/recall driver, so every "GPU-arm" fidelity cell
silently ran at the runtime's CPU default, and X8's byte-identity was
CPU-versus-CPU. The fix and its red-first regression test are merged. What
remains is to spend the fix: the GPU fidelity cells measured for real, X8 at
full coverage, and GPU-corrected throughput at the deployed dtypes.

Two findings from 0481 shape the scope. fp32 runs 99,9 % on CUDA and comes
out faster than q8 there, because the quantized matmul has no CUDA kernel and
falls back to CPU — so the optimal rung differs by device, and the menu
entries 0440 proposes may need to say so. And the genuine cross-provider
signature (close, not byte-identical) is what X8's bar was written for; one
candidate has cleared it, five have not been measured.

## Relevant files

- `tickets/0481-...erg` — the mechanism, the evidence paths, the caveats
- `tickets/closed/0264-...erg` — the campaign being corrected
- `bench/sweep.py` — carries the fix; use it as merged
- `bench/results/0264-gpu-arm/` — fidelity figures superseded by this run;
  state the supersession where they are cited
- `verification/probes/gpu_anomaly_embed_probe.mjs` — the device-forwarding
  probe pattern
- `spec/DESIGN.md` §3 X8 — the decision rule and the bar

## Actions

1. On padme (llama-server stop/restart per the standing authorization and
   0481's procedure), re-run the fidelity cells for every candidate at every
   rung loadable under an explicit GPU device, with the fixed harness. Use
   explicit `cuda` where `auto` crashes per 0481/0264 (the granite models).
2. Score X8 per candidate at every shared rung against 0263's CPU vectors —
   the genuine cross-provider comparison this time; report against DESIGN §3's
   bar.
3. Measure GPU throughput at the rungs 0267 could actually deploy (fp32 and
   the 8-bit rungs), so R30's bound can derive from the recommended
   candidate's real figure.
4. Mark the superseded 0264 fidelity figures as superseded where cited, never
   rewriting the artifacts.

## Test

- The harness's device regression test already gates this; additionally the
  campaign's own vector metadata must record the resolved device, not
  "(runtime default)" — assert it per cell before scoring.

## Verification

- [ ] No fidelity result in this campaign records "(runtime default)" as its
      device
- [ ] X8 reported per candidate and rung, with the bar stated
- [ ] The 0264 fidelity figures are marked superseded where cited

## Invariants

- No 0263/0264 artifact is rewritten; supersession is stated beside citations
- Warm only; repeats with spread for anything ranked
- llama-server's state recorded before and after

## Exit criteria

- [ ] GPU fidelity cells re-measured for every candidate at every loadable
      rung, device asserted per cell
- [ ] X8 at full coverage with a verdict per candidate
- [ ] GPU-corrected throughput for the deployable rungs, ready for 0267 and
      R30's bound
